cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Covert Channel Studio
message: >-
  If you use this educational lab in teaching or research, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: systemslibrarian (Covert Channel Studio contributors)
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/systemslibrarian/crypto-lab-covert-channel-studio
url: >-
  https://systemslibrarian.github.io/crypto-lab-covert-channel-studio/
abstract: >-
  An educational, fully-simulated Crypto-Lab exhibit on covert channels: hidden
  communication in protocols, timing, and media. It teaches storage vs. timing
  channels, DNS/HTTP/IP-field/ordering/steganography carriers, the
  capacity/reliability/observability trade-off, and how defenders detect them
  using named, cited statistical methods — with a blind detection challenge and
  a detector validation lab. It runs entirely client-side and generates no real
  network traffic.
keywords:
  - covert channels
  - security education
  - steganography
  - timing channel
  - dns tunneling
  - steganalysis
  - detection
  - crypto-lab
